Version control systems are specialized software tools that manage changes to source code and digital assets over time. They enable multiple developers to collaborate simultaneously, track revisions, revert modifications, and maintain an immutable audit trail of contributions. Core functionalities include branching, merging, conflict resolution, and seamless integration with continuous integration pipelines.
