What is a Version Control System?
Version Control System (VCS) is a foundational tool in modern software development, enabling teams to manage source code evolution efficiently. By storing code snapshots as a series of revisions, VCS solutions provide traceability, rollback capabilities, and collaborative workflows that underpin continuous delivery pipelines.
Beyond software engineering, VCS tools are increasingly leveraged in configuration management, data science, and hardware design, where managing large binaries and complex dependency graphs is critical.
